# ── Production ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Loaded by `vite build` (mode: production) — i.e. `pnpm run build:web` and
# `pnpm run deploy:web`.
#
# Committed on purpose, and this is the file that has to be right: these values
# are baked into the bundle at build time, so a wrong one ships to the live site
# and cannot be corrected without a rebuild. There are no secrets here — a
# build-time VITE_ variable is public by definition, visible to anyone who reads
# the JavaScript. Real secrets live in the Render dashboard, server side.
#
# Deploys are run from a developer's machine (see render.yaml — the frontend is
# not built by CI), which is exactly why these live in the repo instead of in a
# local file: the deployed bundle should not depend on whose laptop built it.

# The Render service. Also inlined into index.html's preconnect and the
# in-<head> content prefetch.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://prime-developers-api.onrender.com

# Preconnect hint only — the public storage buckets that serve images and .glb
# models. No credentials.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://nrtqntqutquapydsnjbm.supabase.co

# DEV_API_TARGET is deliberately absent: the dev-server proxy does not exist in
# a build, and setting it here would only be misleading.
